    "title": "<p>A comparison of the TNM staging systems in the eighth-edition Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) and American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) classifications</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Daniel Maurice Berney",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 100.0%; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 17.25pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.25pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pathological feature</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.25pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>UICC eighth edition</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.25pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>AJCC eighth edition</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 15.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Rete testis invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 15.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Size of tumour</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">No size criteria used</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">30&nbsp;mm used as a cut-off point&nbsp;(between pT1a and pT1b), for seminoma only</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 15.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Epididymal invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 15.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Tunica vaginalis invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 15.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Vascular invasion </strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 15.0pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 13.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Soft tissue invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">Not considered</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 13.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 20.32%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt;\" width=\"20%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Cord invasion</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT3 but no definition given</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 39.84%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 13.5pt;\" width=\"39%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">pT3 with criteria on level of invasion above the insertion of the tunica vaginalis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
